oscompat is a C library that provides POSIX style helpers on Linux and Windows

POSIX is the reference
Each platform uses a native backend so the same source behaves the same way

The public header is oscompat.h
The library is a static archive

Linux and Windows are supported
macOS is not supported because WrapDL needs Linux ELF interfaces

Notes

Path handling uses the host separator
On Windows both slash and backslash are accepted
os_getopt and os_getopt_long follow POSIX getopt
Scanning stops at the first non option and argv is never permuted
Failures are reported through the return value and errno
On Windows os_set_system_error maps the Win32 error code to errno
Contributions are welcome

